<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    Tool shell styles — the repeated chrome recipes of the rebuilt Pre-Build tool
    pages (action-strip buttons, section cards, band borders, the recurring text
    tiers), lifted from the two hand-rolled reference pages so twelve pages stop
    re-declaring the same six setters.

    ══════════════ THREE HARD CONSTRAINTS, ALL LOAD-BEARING ══════════════

    1. KEYED STYLES ONLY. Every Style in this file carries an x:Key and therefore
       applies to nothing until a page asks for it by name. There is not one
       implicit (TargetType-only) Style here, and none may be added.

       This is not tidiness. The sibling dictionary ToolControlStyles.xaml
       documents the incident in place (see its closing comment): a single
       implicit `Style TargetType="Expander" BasedOn="{StaticResource
       DefaultExpanderStyle}"` hard-crashed the app on FIRST tab realization —
       the framework default style materialized a full ControlTemplate lazily, at
       the moment the tab was first built, on a control that existed nowhere else
       in the app. A red build would have been a gift; instead it was a crash on
       first open.

    2. NO BasedOn ANYWHERE — not even keyed-on-keyed. Two of the styles below
       (secondary and danger) are chrome-identical and BasedOn would express that
       in one line, but this dictionary is the foundation eight panel lanes build
       on and the failure mode above is a first-open crash, not a build error.
       The setters are repeated instead. Deliberate duplication; do not "clean it
       up".

    3. MERGED PER-VIEW, NEVER INTO App.xaml. Hub.WinUI hosts the embedded
       Architect + Visualist pillar views in the same process. An app-wide
       dictionary would reach their subtrees too, violating the per-pillar
       chrome-independence rule, and would re-arm constraint 1 process-wide.
       Merge it in each consuming view's <UserControl.Resources>:

           <ResourceDictionary Source="ms-appx:///Panels/Common/ToolShellStyles.xaml" />

    A NOTE ON KEYS: StaticResource resolves at PARSE time against the merge chain
    (this dictionary → the consuming view → app resources). A mistyped key here
    is a hard XAML parse failure when the tool view is realized — a first-open
    crash, not a red build. Every theme key referenced below (SansFont, MonoFont,
    Radius1Corner, the Coal/Ember brushes) is defined in PhoenixDark.xaml, which
    App.xaml merges app-wide.
-->
<ResourceDictionary
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════ Brushes ══════════════════════════════ -->

    <!--
        Brass hero gradient for the primary CTA. Identical to the page-local
        GvBrassHeroBrush / TmBrassHeroBrush the two reference pages declare; it
        lives here so ToolBrassCtaStyle can carry its own fill and a page that
        uses the style cannot end up with a default Fluent button ground by
        forgetting to set Background. Pages that keep their own local copy are
        unaffected — the gradients are the same four stops.
    -->
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="ToolBrassHeroBrush" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
        <GradientStop Offset="0.00" Color="#F0B463" />
        <GradientStop Offset="0.30" Color="#E5A24E" />
        <GradientStop Offset="0.70" Color="#C8822B" />
        <GradientStop Offset="1.00" Color="#A6661A" />
    </LinearGradientBrush>

    <!-- Overlay / flyout scrim — coal at ~0.78 alpha. -->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ToolScrimBrush" Color="#C70B0907" />

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════ Buttons ══════════════════════════════
         All four share the reference's 30px height so an action strip lines up
         on one baseline. None of them sets Foreground: the house buttons paint
         their label on the inner TextBlock / FontIcon (GiveawayView.xaml:311-318),
         which is immune to the framework template's per-visual-state foreground
         overrides. A Foreground setter here would be silently stomped on hover. -->

    <!-- Neutral action. The strip's default verb (ADD …, REFRESH, EXPORT …). -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolSecondaryButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="30" />
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="14,0" />
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource CoalCardBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource CoalDividerBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource Radius1Corner}" />
    </Style>

    <!--
        Destructive action — strip column 5, at most one per strip.

        Chrome-identical to ToolSecondaryButtonStyle ON PURPOSE. The house does
        not paint destructive buttons red: only the GLYPH turns red, and it does
        so on the caller's FontIcon (TimerView.xaml:324-325 — Foreground
        ErrBrush on the icon, CoalBodyTextBrush on the label, CoalCard ground).
        The key exists so a lane can name its intent, and so this comment has
        somewhere to live.
    -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolDangerButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="30" />
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="14,0" />
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource CoalCardBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource CoalDividerBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource Radius1Corner}" />
    </Style>

    <!--
        Brass primary CTA — EXACTLY ONE per visible surface. Paint the inner
        label and glyph CoalShellBrush (see ToolBrassCtaLabelTextStyle).

        Note this is NOT the theme's EmberPrimaryButtonStyle, which is a flat
        EmberShadow fill at a different padding, spacing and no fixed height.
    -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolBrassCtaStyle" TargetType="Button">
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="30" />
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="14,0" />
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource ToolBrassHeroBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource Ember600Brush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource Radius1Corner}" />
    </Style>

    <!--
        Chip host — the master-enable button that wraps a TogglePill
        (TimerView.xaml:281-291). Asymmetric padding: the pill sits closer to the
        left edge than the label does to the right.
    -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolChipButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
        <Setter Property="Height" Value="30" />
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="10,0,12,0" />
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource CoalCardBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource CoalDividerBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource Radius1Corner}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════ Surfaces ══════════════════════════════ -->

    <!--
        Detail-column section card. CoalShell is DARKER than the page ground
        (CoalSurface), with an opaque CoalCard border — the card recedes, it does
        not raise. Padding 14,10 per GiveawayView.xaml:464-468.
    -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolSectionCardStyle" TargetType="Border">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource CoalShellBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource CoalCardBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource Radius1Corner}" />
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="14,10" />
    </Style>

    <!--
        Full-width band with a bottom hairline — the pinned state band above a
        gated detail scroller, and the column band above a list.

        ★ Do NOT bind IsEnabled on a Border carrying this style. IsEnabled is
        declared on Control, not on UIElement as it is in WPF; binding it on a
        Border / Grid / StackPanel kills the XAML markup compiler with a bare
        MSB3073 and no diagnostic at any verbosity. Gate the enclosing
        ScrollViewer instead.
    -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolBandBorderStyle" TargetType="Border">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource CoalRaisedBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource CoalDividerBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0,0,0,1" />
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="14,6" />
    </Style>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════ Text tiers ══════════════════════════════
         The five recurring text recipes in the reference pages. Sizes and
         spacings are the reference's, not new values. -->

    <!-- Card / section eyebrow: small ember caps. -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolEyebrowTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource SansFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
        <Setter Property="CharacterSpacing" Value="180" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource EmberPrimaryBrush}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Settings-row label, left column. Wraps, because the label column is a
         fixed 150px and several labels are sentences. -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolSettingsLabelTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource MonoFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
        <Setter Property="CharacterSpacing" Value="40" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Action-strip button label (neutral + danger buttons). -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolStripLabelTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource SansFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold" />
        <Setter Property="CharacterSpacing" Value="100" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource CoalBodyTextBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Brass CTA label — coal ON brass, the one inverted text tier. -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolBrassCtaLabelTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource SansFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold" />
        <Setter Property="CharacterSpacing" Value="100" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource CoalShellBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Mono body: values, list cells, the pinned state sentence. -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolMonoBodyTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource MonoFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource CoalPrimaryTextBrush}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Mono hint: the quiet explanatory line under a field.
         Row-hint variant: same recipe with VerticalAlignment="Center" set
         INLINE at the call site. Three pages had forked a whole style for
         that one setter; a local override is cheaper than a fourth key. -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolMonoHintTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource MonoFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══════════════ 2026-08-14 — the missing tiers ═══════════════

         Majo, on 1.1.9: the Pre-Build pages "are NOT conclusive and overall do
         not look like they were made from the same person."

         Measured rather than eyeballed: EIGHT distinct field-label recipes were
         live across the fourteen panels, and twenty-one of the declarations
         carrying them were page-local copies of five signatures. Not variation
         with intent — the same setters, retyped per page under a per-page name
         (AlSubLabel / LoySubLabel / PlStripCaption / QtStripCaption /
         RkStripCaption / SrStripCaption / UmSubLabel are byte-identical).

         The cause is structural, not sloppiness: this dictionary shipped the
         chrome tiers (buttons, cards, bands) but never the FORM interior tiers,
         so every lane that had to label a field invented one and named it after
         its page. The 1.1.7 parity rebuild put all twelve panels on the house
         chrome and left the interiors untouched, which is exactly why the pages
         still read as several authors after it.

         The five keys below are those five signatures, promoted verbatim — no
         redesign, no new look, so adopting them is a pure rename with zero
         visual delta. Constraints 1-3 in the header still apply: keyed, no
         BasedOn, merged per view.
    -->

    <!-- Sub-label / strip caption: mono caps under a stat or beside a control.
         Was: AlSubLabel, LoySubLabel, PlStripCaption, QtStripCaption,
         RkStripCaption, SrStripCaption, UmSubLabel (7 identical copies). -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolSubLabelTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource MonoFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
        <Setter Property="CharacterSpacing" Value="120" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Explanatory hint, sans tier. The muted foreground is what separates it
         from ToolMonoHintTextStyle: this one is prose, that one is a value note.
         Was: PlHint, RkHint, SrHint, SbHint (4 identical copies). -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolHintTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource SansFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource CoalMutedTextBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
    </Style>

    <!-- List/table column header. Set VerticalAlignment="Center" inline where
         the column header sits in a centred cell — two pages had forked the
         whole style for that single setter.
         Was: AlBandLabel, AmColumnLabel, LoyColHeader, CcColumnCaption,
         QtColumnCaption (5 copies across 2 near-identical signatures). -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolColumnLabelTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource SansFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="9" />
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold" />
        <Setter Property="CharacterSpacing" Value="140" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Empty-state headline. The one place DisplayFont is legitimate inside a
         panel body, and it is deliberately the SECONDARY foreground so an
         absence never outranks live content.
         Was: AmEmptyTitle, LoyEmptyTitle (2 identical copies). -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolEmptyTitleTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource DisplayFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="20" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Center" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Inline warning line (a collision, a disabled dependency).
         Was: PlWarn, SbWarn (2 identical copies). -->
    <Style x:Key="ToolWarnTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource SansFont}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource ErrBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══════════════ Input widths — the recipe that never existed ═══════════

         The audited gap: nothing in either tool dictionary described input
         GEOMETRY, so every lane guessed. A four-character verb ended up in a
         star-stretched box while a two-digit number sat in a 64 px one, at a
         different height, on the same page.

         These are widths ONLY, deliberately. ToolControlStyles.xaml already
         owns TextBox chrome through an implicit style plus the TextControl*
         brushes; adding colour or border here would put two dictionaries in
         competition over the same control. Width encodes expected content:

             Xs  integers, percents, seconds
             Sm  command verbs, single tokens, dropdowns
             Md  names, queue names, group names

         Anything wider is a message template and should stretch, not take a
         token. Applied as Width="{StaticResource ToolFieldWidthSm}".
    -->
    <x:Double x:Key="ToolFieldWidthXs">84</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="ToolFieldWidthSm">150</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="ToolFieldWidthMd">260</x:Double>

</ResourceDictionary>
